WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:09.000
Today, Web DSH, Web Terminal, and installed managed clients operate in the user's private workspace.

00:09.000 --> 00:19.000
DSH chat does not forward work to another client. A reviewed source candidate adds an Agent tasks page.

00:19.000 --> 00:29.000
It separates agent runtime from execution backend and offers DSH Python SDK, Claude Code, and Deep Agents.

00:29.000 --> 00:40.000
Every task requires approval, stays in a private project, streams persisted output, and supports cancellation and interrupted recovery.

00:40.000 --> 00:50.000
OpenShell is optional, disabled, and unavailable until its isolation, rollback, resource, and expiry gates pass.

00:50.000 --> 01:00.000
The candidate is not deployed. Build, bounded live acceptance, digest verification, and spoken-content review remain.
